data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:19:21.689774+00:00", "content": "Based on my investigation, I've gathered substantial evidence about the `ce_branch24` situation. Here's a summary you can use to create a well-documented Jira ticket:\n\n---\n\n## **Investigation Summary: ce_branch24 SD-WAN Tunnel Degradation**\n\n### **Primary Issue: Tunnel to `ce_hub3` experiencing ~50% packet loss** [metrics:98]\n- **`ce_branch24` \u2192 `ce_hub3` tunnel**: **49.81% loss**, 0.87ms jitter, 75.7ms latency\n- **All other 5 tunnels** (to ce_hub1,2,4,5,6): **<0.11% loss**, 0.8-13ms jitter, 60-75ms latency [metrics:84-101]\n\n### **Correlated Instability Indicators**\n- **Tunnel rekeys**: `ce_hub3` tunnel shows **10 rekeys** vs **3 rekeys** for all other tunnels [metrics:102-107] \u2014 indicates repeated tunnel renegotiation/flapping\n- **Interface `eth0` congestion**: 88 queue drops [metrics:6] + 1,877 input discards [metrics:26] \u2014 suggests upstream congestion on the primary WAN link\n- **All interfaces operationally UP** [metrics:53-61] \u2014 no hard link failures\n\n### **Topology Context** [topo:ce_branch24]\n- **Direct neighbors (hop 1)**: `h_branch24_corp`, `h_branch24_voice` (no metrics), `pe12` (healthy \u2014 BGP/OSPF/MPLS all established)\n- **Downstream (hop 2)**: `ce_branch12` (healthy, similar SD-WAN metrics), `p23`, `p24` (core routers, healthy)\n- **Blast radius appears limited** to the `ce_hub3` path; other hubs and local services unaffected\n\n### **Healthy Metrics**\n- Hardware: fan 3000 RPM, temp 28.9\u00b0C, PSU 11.9V \u2014 all normal [metrics:0-3]\n- CPU 0.56%, Memory 19% \u2014 no resource pressure [metrics:80-81]\n- SD-WAN paths for CORP/VOICE VRFs: **active** [metrics:82-83]\n- Transceiver: RX -5.8 dBm, temp 37\u00b0C, bias 28.3mA \u2014 within spec [metrics:108-110]\n\n---\n\n### **Suggested Jira Ticket Fields**\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Summary** | `ce_branch24`: SD-WAN tunnel to `ce_hub3` at ~50% packet loss (10 rekeys), other 5 tunnels healthy |\n| **Severity** | Major (P2) \u2014 single-hub path degraded, but redundancy via 5 other hubs |\n| **Component** | SD-WAN / WAN Edge |\n| **Affected Device** | `ce_branch24` (branch), tunnel `ce_branch24-ce_hub3` |\n| **Evidence** | Metrics citations: [metrics:98] (49.8% loss), [metrics:104] (10 rekeys), [metrics:6] (eth0 queue drops), [metrics:26] (eth0 input discards), [metrics:84-101] (healthy comparison tunnels), [topo:ce_branch24] (topology context) |\n| **Next Steps** | 1. Check `ce_hub3` health / path MTU / underlay to that hub<br>2. Verify `eth0` upstream provider link (congestion signs)<br>3. Review tunnel config asymmetry (why only hub3 affected?)<br>4. Correlate with any recent changes on hub3 path |\n\n---\n\n**Note**: I cannot create the Jira ticket directly (read-only investigator), but the evidence above is ready to paste into your ticketing system. Would you like me to dig deeper into any specific aspect \u2014 e.g., query `ce_hub3` metrics, check historical trends, or search for similar past incidents once the backend recovers?"}

